# ── dependencies and build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
# ...and as a bare symlink. Agents working in a git worktree link these two in
# rather than reinstalling, and a trailing-slash pattern does not match a
# symlink, so both got committed once already.
node_modules
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── capture harness output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# shots/ is where every tool writes its frames. It is ~2.8 GB and every file in
# it is regenerable with `node tools/shot.mjs`, so it stays out of history.
shots/

# review/ holds the archived contact sheets the art director judges rounds from.
# The IMAGES are no longer tracked: 94 of them were 163 MB, against a 23 MB src/
# tree, and unlike the bakes they were all live — no amount of history rewriting
# would have recovered that, because none of it was stale. They stay on local
# disk and are written by tools/review.mjs as before.
#
# The text in review/ IS still tracked, and deliberately so: review/INDEX.md is
# the numbered written record of every round, review/anchors.json is read by
# tools/postsweep.mjs, tod.mjs, clouddrift.mjs and cloudprobe.mjs, and
# review/perf/*.json are measurements cited from docs/PERF_FINDINGS.md. Together
# they are ~104 KB. Losing the images costs the pictures; losing these would
# break the harnesses and the record of what was decided.
#
# Archive the images off-repo if they need to outlive this working copy.
review/**/*.png
review/**/*.jpg
review/*.png
review/*.jpg

# reference-art/ is deliberately TRACKED: it is the art target every visual
# judgement is measured against. Do not add it here, and do not delete from it.

# ── world bakes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# public/bakes/ is generated, not source. Run `node tools/bake.mjs` once after
# cloning; it writes the .pab bakes and manifest.json in ~25 s per resolution.
#
# These were tracked until 2026-08-21, on the reasoning that a fresh clone
# should run without waiting for a bake. That trade stopped being worth it:
#
#   * Nothing needs git to carry them. The Vercel build regenerates them from
#     source (`node tools/bake.mjs` in vercel.json's buildCommand) and ships
#     them in dist/, and a client with no bake at all bakes live in a worker
#     (src/main.js — `loadCachedBake() ?? bakeWorld()`). The tracked copies
#     only ever saved *developers* the one-time bake.
#   * They cost 387 MB of the 637 MB .git. Every edit to TerrainGen.js changes
#     the generator hash and produces a whole new 44 MB incompressible blob.
#     tools/bake.mjs prunes stale bakes from disk correctly, but git history
#     keeps every generation forever regardless of the delete.
#
# So: 25 s of CPU once per clone, against a repository nobody could clone.
public/bakes/
public/bakes

# ── local noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ── scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tools/_scratch/ holds one-off diagnostic instruments and IS tracked — several
# of them (cost2, tierload, wdrive's ancestors) are load-bearing. Only their
# output is ignored.
tools/_scratch/**/out/
tools/_scratch/**/*.png

# Blender writes a .blend1 rollback beside every save; it is not source.
*.blend1
